cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "habRAG: 奥匈帝国史研究助手"
abstract: >-
  A retrieval-augmented research assistant for Habsburg and Austro-Hungarian
  history. Performs hybrid retrieval (dense vector search fused with lexical
  BM25 / FTS5 search via RRF, followed by reranking) over a corpus of 160,475
  passages drawn from 190 works in English, German, Polish and Chinese, of which
  21.6% are primary archival sources (ÖUA, MRP, Conrad memoirs). Designed around
  citation verifiability: generated answers carry machine-checkable citations in
  two formats (secondary literature and archival document numbers), and long
  documents can be verified claim-by-claim through an agentic tool loop.
authors:
